            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "'mini.ai' works using [Lua patterns](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/5df3155218807fb6049779bb488f48f77fdd9dcb/doc/mini-ai.txt#L44-L45) which are not designed to deliver 100% compatibility with parsing structured nested data.\r\n\r\nIf there is a concrete example of something not working as expected, please provide a step-by-step reproducible example. The attached video is not reproducible for me. Also, chances are that this was already [discussed in one of the previous issues](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues?q=label%3Amini.ai+tag).\r\n\r\nIf you want to disable particular built-in textobject, you can disable it by setting to `false` entry in `custom_textobjects`. [Like this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/5df3155218807fb6049779bb488f48f77fdd9dcb/doc/mini-ai.txt#L450-L451).\r\n\r\nClosing as there is not enough information.",
